---
import SiteLayout from "@/layouts/SiteLayout.astro";
---

<SiteLayout
  title="Get started with Agent Toolkit"
  description="Install the portable Agent Toolkit CLI, preview your coding-tool targets and choose capabilities with clear provenance."
>
  <section class="page-hero">
    <div class="wrap">
      <p class="eyebrow">Portable capability toolkit</p>
      <h1>Start with the tools you already use.</h1>
      <p class="lede">
        Install the Agent Toolkit CLI, inspect which coding tools and targets it
        supports, then preview the exact changes before applying any
        capabilities.
      </p>
      <div class="button-row">
        <a class="button" href="/docs/installation/">
          Install the CLI
        </a>
        <a class="button secondary" href="/docs/compatibility/">
          Check compatibility
        </a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="section section--deep">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="semantic-list">
        <article class="semantic-item">
          <span class="term">01 · INSTALL</span>
          <p>
            <strong>Choose a supported channel</strong>
            <br />
            Use the native release, PyPI/uv, npm or another documented
            distribution.
          </p>
        </article>
        <article class="semantic-item">
          <span class="term">02 · INSPECT</span>
          <p>
            <strong>Preview target paths</strong>
            <br />
            Check tool support, provenance, conflicts and files before writing.
          </p>
        </article>
        <article class="semantic-item">
          <span class="term">03 · APPLY</span>
          <p>
            <strong>Select what you need</strong>
            <br />
            Install chosen skills, agents or templates while preserving
            user-owned files.
          </p>
        </article>
      </div>
      <div class="migration-note">
        <strong>Need a graphical coding application?</strong>
        <p>
          Veasel Code provides the supported Desktop and TUI experience with one
          canonical runtime.
        </p>
        <a href="https://www.veasel.dev/downloads/">Download Veasel Code ↗</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</SiteLayout>
